# Apartment typologies — `ბ ტიპის ბინა` family

This office ships three apartment types in a townhouse-cluster format
(`bina #N`). Sizes, structural module, walls, doors, windows and
furniture pack are fixed. Use these numbers when generating, validating
or analysing a `bina`.

## Common parameters (all types)

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---|
| Drawing units | mm (`INSUNITS = 4`) |
| Coordinate frame | UTM zone 38 N (Tbilisi) — values in mm × 1 000 of UTM-m |
| Structural module (typical bay) | **6 500 mm** |
| End-bay variant | 6 900 mm |
| Floor-to-floor height | 3 000 mm |
| Floor slab | 200 mm RC |
| External wall | **600 mm** = 300 mm RC + 200 mm insulation + 100 mm finish |
| Internal partition | **400 mm** (heavy block + double plaster) |
| Light partition | 100 mm (drywall, only WC inside-flat) |
| Front door (D2) | **900 × 2 100 mm** |
| Interior door (D1) | **800 × 2 100 mm** |
| Bathroom door (D3) | **700 × 2 100 mm** *(use this — do not reuse D1)* |
| Bathroom vent window (W1) | 700 × 600 mm |
| Bedroom window (W3) | 900 × 1 400 mm (small) or 1 600 × 1 400 mm (large) |
| Kitchen window (W4) | 1 000 × 1 400 mm (project actual) or 1 200 × 1 400 mm (rule 02 default) |
| Living window (W5) | 1 600 × 1 400 mm |
| Balcony door | 1 800 × 2 100 mm or 2 200 × 2 100 mm |

## Type A — small / `პატარა ბინა`

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---|
| Net flat area | **45 – 46 m²** |
| Bedrooms | 1 |
| Living + kitchen | combined L+K |
| Bathroom | 1 (full) |
| Footprint (typical) | 9.30 × 5.80 m |
| Doors | 1 × D2 + 5 × D1 + 1 × D3 |
| Windows | 1 × W4 + 1 × W3 + 1 × W1 + 1 × W5 = 4 |
| Furniture pack | 1 sofa, 1 dining-rectangle, 1 kitchen, 1 bed, 2–3 wardrobes, 1 TV, 1 shelf, 1 bath set |
| Position in cluster | row-2 corners (e.g. `bina #22`, `#25`) |

## Type B — standard / `სტანდარტული ბინა`

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---|
| Net flat area | **63 – 69 m²** (target ≈ 65) |
| Bedrooms | 2 |
| Living | 17.3 m² |
| Master bedroom | 12.1 m² |
| Bedroom | 11.0 m² |
| Kitchen | 8.0 m² |
| Bathroom | 7.9 m² |
| Footprint (typical) | 6.50 × 10.30 m (one structural bay × full depth) |
| Doors | 1 × D2 + 5 × D1 + 1 × D3 |
| Windows | 1 × W4 + 1 × W3 + 1 × W5 + 1 × W1 = 4 (mid units) up to 6 |
| Furniture pack | 1 sofa, 1 dining-rectangle, 1 kitchen, 2 beds, 3 wardrobes, 1 TV, 1 shelf, 1 bath set |
| Position in cluster | mid-row (e.g. `bina #9, #10, #23, #24, #37, #38`) |

## Type C — end-cap / `ბოლო ერთეული`

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---|
| Net flat area | **85 – 86 m²** |
| Bedrooms | 3 |
| Footprint (typical) | 9.54 × 10.30 m |
| Doors | 1 × D2 + 6 × D1 + 2 × D3 |
| Windows | 9 (incl. 2 × W5 living, 2 × W3 bedrooms, 1 × W1 bath) |
| Furniture pack | 1 sofa **set**, 1 round dining, 1 kitchen, 3 beds, 4 wardrobes, 2 baths (full), 1 washer, 1 TV, 1 shelf |
| Position in cluster | row-1 ends (e.g. `bina #8`, `#39`) |

## Cluster geometry

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---|
| Default cluster size | 5 + 5 = 10 binebi |
| Cluster X-span (10 binas) | **54 060 mm** |
| Cluster Y-span (2 rows) | 9 890 mm |
| Cluster envelope | ≈ 535 m² |
| Σ net flat area (10 binas, 1 floor) | **658.4 m²** |
| Mean / median flat | 65.84 / 65.6 m² |

## Generator parameters (for `bina-b-type.lsp`)

```
(setq *bay-x* 6500.0)        ; structural bay width
(setq *depth*  10300.0)      ; full depth (front to back)
(setq *wall-ext* 600.0)
(setq *wall-int* 400.0)
(setq *door-front* 900.0)
(setq *door-int* 800.0)
(setq *door-bath* 700.0)
(setq *win-bedroom* 1600.0)
(setq *win-kitchen* 1000.0)
(setq *win-bath* 700.0)
(setq *floor-h* 3000.0)
```

## Validation thresholds

A generated `bina` passes only when:

- type A: `45 ≤ net m² ≤ 47`
- type B: `63 ≤ net m² ≤ 70`
- type C: `83 ≤ net m² ≤ 88`
- bath area ≥ 3.3 m², kitchen ≥ 6 m², master BR ≥ 12 m², BR ≥ 9 m², living ≥ 16 m² (СНиП 2.07.01-89)
- every door is D1 / D2 / D3 from the table above (no other widths)
- every window is W1–W5 from the table above
